+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+The repository does not contain a recorded full-recall p95 for the adversarial
+synthetic 30-word-vocabulary workload before the term-selection fix. No number is
+reported here for that baseline rather than substituting an estimate.
+
+The fix was to select at most eight prompt terms by inverse document frequency
+(IDF), dropping terms absent from the store and, for stores with at least 50
+active records, terms appearing in more than one third of the store. This keeps
+uninformative high-frequency terms and their long posting lists out of the BM25
+query.
+
+The repository also does not contain a recorded post-fix full-recall p95 tied to
+that specific adversarial synthetic workload. The separately documented
+**4.31 ms p95** is an end-to-end `UserPromptSubmit` measurement on a 50,000-record
+prototype corpus (`research/00-evidence-log.md`, measurement I3); it is not
+identified as the adversarial 30-word-vocabulary result and therefore is not
+used as the post-fix number here.
